    "chunk_text": "4. The Director General may request for further information or documents to be furnished, including anyclarification that he may consider to be necessary for the purpose of deciding such application.\n\n5. An application found to contain false, misleading or incorrect information or particulars shall be rejected.\n\n7. Upon the receipt of an application for the issuance of a license from the registered Tourist Guide Lecturer, theDirector - General may direct the applicant to furnish such further information, documents or clarifications pertaining tothe application within such period as may be specified, for the issuance of license.\n\n8 (1) The Director-General shall, on being satisfied that the applicant possesses the minimum requirements andqualifications specified in the Schedule I and Schedule II hereto as appropriate, issue a license to such applicant to serveas a tourist guide lecturer.\n\n(2) The Director-General shall, inform the applicant of his decision in writing within a period of one monthand in a case of a refusal to issue the license, he shall specify his reasons therefor.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'09'10PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 10.09.20193A\n\n9. The license issued under regulation 8 of these regulations -\n\n(a)may be subject to such terms and condition as specified in the license, which the Director-General maydeem appropriate for securing due compliance with the provisions of Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005 orany regulation made thereunder.\n\n(b)shall come into force on the date specified therein ; and\n\n(c)shall unless it is earlier cancelled or revoked by the Director-General, remain in force for a period ofone year from the date specified in the license.\n\nPART II\n\nGeneral Provisions"
