    "chunk_text": "1AI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'09'10PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 10.09.2019\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2140$33 - 2019 iema;e\u00efn\u00be ui 10 jeks w\u00d5yrejdod - 2019'09'10No. 2140/33 - TUESDAY, SEPTEMBER 10, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERALGovernment Notifications\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n1A- G 30964 - 12(2019/09)\n\nPilgrimages Ordinance\n\nREGULATIONS made by the Minister of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils & Local Government in termsof Section 2 of Pilgrimages Ordinance. (Chap. 175).\n\nWAJIRA ABEYWARDHANA,Internal & Home Affairs andProvincial Councils & Local Government.\n\nMinistry of Internal & Home Affairs and Provincial Councils &Local Government,Nila Medura New Building,Elvitigala Mawatha,Narahenpita,Colombo 05.10th September, 2019.\n\n2AI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'09'10PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 10.09.2019\n\nRegulations\n\n1. These regulations may be cited as the regulation of Perahera of Mihinthale Rajamaha Viharaya, in the GramaNiladaris\u2019s Division of Mihinthale 577, Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Mihinthale, Anuradhapura District.\n\n2.In these regulations:\n\n\u201cCamp area\u201d means the area described in the Schedule..\u201cDistrict Secretary/ Government Agent\u201d means the Government Agent of Anuradhapura Administrative Districtand it also includes any officer authorized by him in terms of regulation 4.\u201cMedical Officer\u201d means the Medical officer in charge of the camp area.\n\n\u201cPilgrim\u201d means any person who enters and stays within the camp area for any purpose.\n\n\u201cPolice Officer\u201d includes any Grama Niladhari in charge of the camp area."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_extraordinary_gazettes_2010s",
