    "language": "en",
    "md5": "aa6757c6819b3c9d575e0576e41f8707",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cCamp area\u201d means the area described in the Schedule..\u201cDistrict Secretary/ Government Agent\u201d means the Government Agent of Anuradhapura Administrative Districtand it also includes any officer authorized by him in terms of regulation 4.\u201cMedical Officer\u201d means the Medical officer in charge of the camp area.\n\n\u201cPilgrim\u201d means any person who enters and stays within the camp area for any purpose.\n\n\u201cPolice Officer\u201d includes any Grama Niladhari in charge of the camp area.\n\n3.These regulations shall apply to the pilgrimages made on account of the Perahera festival of Mihinthale RajamahaViharaya in the Grama Niladaris\u2019s Division of Mihinthale 577, Divisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Mihinthale,Anuradhapura District.\n\n4.The District Secretary/ Government Agent shall have the power to authorize any public officer in writing toexercise any power vested in him and carry out any function assigned to him under this regulation.\n\n5.I. The District Secretary/ Government Agent shall have the power to regulate vehicular traffic or walking to orfrom or within the camp area.\n\nII. No person shall act contrary to any lawful order given by any police officer in compliance with the instructions issued to such police officer by the District Secretary/ Government Agent for the exercise of powers vested in him under the Para (1) of this regulation.\n\n6.No person shall bring any cattle or any other animal into the camp area without the written permission of theDistrict Secretary/ Government Agent. However, this regulation shall not apply in instance where carts arebrought and cattle are driven to a place reserved for the purpose of leaving carts and cattle, under regulation 7.\n\n7.(1) The District Secretary/ Government Agent shall have the power to reserve or provide the following places inside the camp area."
  },
